# materials.pdl - D35 step M1 (BOOK 16.game/MATERIAL-ATTENTION-AND-EXPERT-MIX-GENERATOR-DESIGN-2026-11-05.md). A material is a COMPOSITION; its base colour is DERIVED, never typed:
#   metal/alloy components are element symbols -> the periodic-element Drude colour (_shared-lib/material_colour.c) unless a PIGMENT row overrides that key;
#   every other component is a formula with a PIGMENT row. Components are mixed by fraction in LINEAR light (gamma 2.2), not by averaging hex.
# PIGMENT | key | hex | reflectance 0..1 | source        source=DOC means a hand estimate by the agent, NOT a measurement. Edit freely; the studio shows derived next to the hand colour.
# MATERIAL | name | class metal|alloy|ceramic|mineral|organic|ice | components key:fraction,... | recipe (the ground.pdl recipe it stands for, or -) | note
PIGMENT | Fe2O3    | #8e3b2a | 0.25 | DOC iron(III) oxide, brick and tile red
PIGMENT | FeOOH    | #a8742c | 0.30 | DOC goethite, ochre and rust
